    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily into favorable matchups against vulnerable starters, headlined by **Cal Raleigh** (72.64) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (72.66). **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Springs, where a combination of lineup placement and strong platoon splits elevates his output. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** (71.62) offers elite stability; while the opposing starter presents a marginal risk for stolen base opportunities, his efficiency remains rock solid due to an ideal park factor and platoon advantage. We are also capitalizing on high-ceiling leadoff spots for **Taylor Ward** (64.85) and **Luis Arraez** (64.37), both of whom are positioned to maximize our R and AVG contributions against favorable arms.\n\nThe decision to bench **Tyler Freeman** (51.83) was the most difficult call of the morning. While he holds a strong score, he narrowly missed the cut because the projected efficiency of the starters\u2014particularly in the utility and outfield slots\u2014offered higher reliability in volume and category coverage. Our biggest risk today involves **Jonathan Aranda** (52.24); while his platoon edge is significant, he is staring down a tough assignment against Cease (2.96 xERA), requiring us to temper expectations for his total output. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **JJ Bleday**, whose score of 39.97 placed him just below our 40-point floor; he remains the primary bench option should any late-breaking lineup changes force a pivot. Keep an eye on **Gleyber Torres** (57.66); while his raw projection is moderate, the wind-out conditions at his park provide a tangible bump that could pay dividends for HR potential.",
